# Full Tenant-Based Routing Migration

Migrate every page from root-based routing (`/admin/courses`) to tenant-based routing (`/[tenantSlug]/admin/courses`). The tenant slug becomes the first path segment for **all** authenticated and most public routes.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a **large architectural refactor** touching 50+ files. The middleware will no longer rewrite/strip slugs — instead, Next.js App Router will natively resolve the `[tenantSlug]` dynamic segment. This is fundamentally different from the current approach.

## Current Architecture vs Target

| Layer | Current | Target |
|---|---|---|
| App Router | `app/(admin)/admin/*`, `app/(dashboard)/*`, `app/(instructor)/instructor/*` | `app/[tenantSlug]/(admin)/admin/*`, `app/[tenantSlug]/(dashboard)/*`, `app/[tenantSlug]/(instructor)/instructor/*` |
| Middleware | Strips slug via rewrite (`/bce/admin` → `/admin`) | Passes through natively (`/bce/admin` resolves to `app/[tenantSlug]/(admin)/admin`) |
| Links | Relative `/admin/courses`, prefixed by [TenantLink](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/lib/tenant/TenantProvider.tsx#60-77) context | Direct `/${tenantSlug}/admin/courses` via `routes.ts` helper |
| Auth redirect | Server Action reads headers → `baseUrl + /admin` | Server Action reads headers → `/${slug}/admin` |

