## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure

---

#### [NEW] [routes.ts](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/lib/routes.ts)
Centralized route helper with typed functions:
```ts
export const routes = {
  admin: (t: string) => `/${t}/admin`,
  adminCourses: (t: string) => `/${t}/admin/courses`,
  dashboard: (t: string) => `/${t}/dashboard`,
  courses: (t: string) => `/${t}/courses`,
  // ... every route
}
```

#### [MODIFY] [middleware.ts](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/middleware.ts)
- **Remove** `RESERVED_FIRST_SEGMENTS` blocklist and the rewrite logic
- Middleware will **only** extract slug + inject headers (`x-tenant-slug`, `x-tenant-id`, `x-routing-mode`)
- No more `NextResponse.rewrite()` — the App Router natively handles `[tenantSlug]`
- Add backward-compat: if user hits bare `/admin`, look up their profile's institution and redirect to `/${slug}/admin`

#### [MODIFY] [tenantResolver.ts](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/lib/tenant/tenantResolver.ts)
- [generateTenantBaseUrl()](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/lib/tenant/tenantResolver.ts#28-32) always returns `/${slug}` regardless of routing mode (dev/wildcard/custom all use path-based now)

#### [MODIFY] [TenantProvider.tsx](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/lib/tenant/TenantProvider.tsx)
- Add `tenantSlug` and `tenantId` to context (currently only exposes `baseUrl`)
- [useTenant()](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/lib/tenant/TenantProvider.tsx#48-51) returns `{ tenantSlug, tenantId, tenant, baseUrl }`

